DNS: The internets phone book 

When you type google.com, you aren't connecting to "google.com".

You're ultimately connecting to an IP address. DNS is the system that makes that translation possible. DNS isn't just about A records.

You should understand:
A → IPv4
AAAA → IPv6
CNAME → Alias
MX → Mail server
TXT → Verification/metadata

For DevOps engineers, DNS knowledge becomes especially important when debugging:
"The application is down."
"The domain isn't resolving."
"The new service isn't reachable."
